General setup information
*************************

We recommend using the NCAlgebra package with the most recent version of
Macaulay2.

Many of the methods in the NCAlgebra package rely on J. Backelin's
noncommutative Groebner basis program Bergman. In the future, we may add
support for other programs which compute Groebner bases, but for now, users
must have Bergman installed.

Detailed instructions for installing Bergman, as well as the NCAlgebra system,
can be found in the file installNCAlgebra.txt file contained in the NCAlgebra
package directory. It may also be found at
https://github.com/Macaulay2/M2/blob/stable/M2/Macaulay2/packages/NCAlgebra/
installNCAlgebra.txt.

See also
========

  * *note Using the Bergman interface: Using the Bergman interface,
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

