coordinates -- Computes coordinates relative to a given basis
*************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        coordinates L
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement: NCRingElement,, or a
        *note List: (Macaulay2Doc)List, of NCRingElements
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Basis => a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value null, a list
        of homogeneous elements to use as a basis for computing coordinate
        vectors
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

Generally, linear algebra in graded rings is performed using the monomial basis
obtained from a Groebner basis calculation. In some cases, it is desirable to
work relative to a different basis. This method calls *note sparseCoeffs:
sparseCoeffs, to compute the coordinate vector(s) of a ring element (or a list
of ring elements) relative to a user-specified basis. If no basis is specified,
the method simple calls *note sparseCoeffs: sparseCoeffs, with no options.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[w]/ideal(w^2+w+1)                       |
|                                                    |
|o1 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = skewPolynomialRing(R,promote(-1,R),{x,y,z})|
|                                                    |
|o2 = A                                              |
|                                                    |
|o2 : NCQuotientRing                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+

One motivating example comes from invariant theory. In this example, we take a
skew polynomial ring in three variables and act by the cyclic subgroup of
graded automorphisms of A generated by permuting the variables. A basis for the
fixed ring is given by "orbit sums" of basis monomials. Here we work in
homogeneous degree 3.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : g = ncMap(A,A,{y,z,x})                                      |
|                                                                 |
|o3 = NCRingMap A <--- A                                          |
|                                                                 |
|o3 : NCRingMap                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : gList = {g, g^2, g^3}                                       |
|                                                                 |
|o4 = {NCRingMap A <--- A, NCRingMap A <--- A, NCRingMap A <--- A}|
|                                                                 |
|o4 : List                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : a = sum apply(3,i-> (gList#i)(x^3))                         |
|                                                                 |
|      3  3  3                                                    |
|o5 = z +y +x                                                     |
|                                                                 |
|o5 : A                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : b = sum apply(3,i-> (gList#i)(x^2*y))                       |
|                                                                 |
|      2    2  2                                                  |
|o6 = y z+xz +x y                                                 |
|                                                                 |
|o6 : A                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : c = sum apply(3,i-> (gList#i)(x*y^2))                       |
|                                                                 |
|       2   2  2                                                  |
|o7 = yz +xy +x z                                                 |
|                                                                 |
|o7 : A                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : d = sum apply(3,i-> (gList#i)(x*y*z))                       |
|                                                                 |
|o8 = 3xyz                                                        |
|                                                                 |
|o8 : A                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------+

It is clear that these are linearly independent. Next, we take a homogeneous
polynomial of degree 3, make it invariant, and compute its coordinate vector.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : p = w^2*z^2*y+x^2*z+(1-w)*y^3                         |
|                                                           |
|                2           3  2                           |
|o9 = (- w - 1)yz +(- w + 1)y +x z                          |
|                                                           |
|o9 : A                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : g(p)==p                                              |
|                                                           |
|o10 = false                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : p' = sum apply(3,i-> (gList#i)(p))                   |
|                                                           |
|                3     2           3     2    2            3|
|o11 = (- w + 1)z +-wyz +(- w + 1)y +-wxy +-wx z+(- w + 1)x |
|                                                           |
|o11 : A                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : g(p')==p'                                            |
|                                                           |
|o12 = true                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : coordinates(p',Basis=>{a,b,c,d})                     |
|                                                           |
|o13 = | -w+1 |                                             |
|      | 0    |                                             |
|      | -w   |                                             |
|      | 0    |                                             |
|                                                           |
|              4      1                                     |
|o13 : Matrix R  <-- R                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note sparseCoeffs: sparseCoeffs, -- Converts ring elements into vectors
    over the coefficient ring

