fourDimSklyanin -- Defines a four-dimensional Sklyanin with given parameters
****************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        fourDimSklyanin(R,params,varList)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 
      * params, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * varList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * DegreeLimit (missing documentation) => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 5,
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, 

Description
===========

This method constructs a three dimensional Sklyanin algebra with parameters
from the params list, and variables from varList (see here (see
https://www.math.washington.edu/~smith/Research/Skly-survey.pdf )). If either
list is not the appropriate length, then an error is thrown.  The generic such
algebra has a fairly complicated Groebner basis, so the optional parameter
DegreeLimit has been defaulted to 5.  If only one list is provided, it is used
for the variable names, and a random choice for each parameter is chosen.

In order to not get a degenerate example, one should ensure that the parameters
provided satisfy \alpha + \beta + \gamma + \alpha\beta\gamma = 0. This method
does not check this condition, since the degenerate examples are of interest as
well.  If no parameters are provided, however a generic choice of \alpha,\beta
and \gamma satisfying the equation above are selected.

