gbFromOutputFile -- Read in a NCGroebnerBasis from a Bergman output file.
*************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Igb = gbFromOutputFile(A,fileName)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note NCPolynomialRing: NCPolynomialRing,, 
      * fileName, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * CacheBergmanGB => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true, specifies whether or not to cache the Groebner
        basis for later use
      * MakeMonic => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, specifies whether the Bergman output should be made monic
      * ReturnIdeal => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false, specifies whether to return an NCIdeal or the
        NCGroebnerBasis
  * Outputs:
      * Igb, an instance of the type *note NCGroebnerBasis: NCGroebnerBasis,,
        or an *note NCIdeal: NCIdeal,

Description
===========

This command reads in a Groebner basis from a Bergman output file. It can be
useful if you have performed a lengthy computation before, and wish to load in
a previously computed result to do some computations.

The Groebner basis we are reading in for this example is located in the
NCAlgebra auxiliary files directory. We are currently unable to compile this
documentation node in a way that enables M2 to read the file. We give a text
version of the session until the issue is resolved.

+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A=QQ{x56,x46,x36,x26,x16,x45,x35,x25,x15,x34,x24,x14,x23,x13,x12}|
|                                                                      |
|o1 = A                                                                |
|                                                                      |
|o1 : NCPolynomialRing                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

I = gbFromOutputFile(A,"NCAlgebra/FK.bo", ReturnIdeal=>true)

B=A/I

hilbertSeries(B,Order=>4)

In "Quadratic algebras, Dunkl elements, and Schubert calculus," Fomin and
Kirillov introduce a family of noncommutative algebras E_n which may be thought
of as the quadratic closure of the ring of "Bruhat operators" acting on a
vector space whose basis is the symmetric group. In that paper, they provide
Hilbert series for the algebras E_1, ..., E_5. The file loaded above is a
Groebner basis of E_6 to degree 6. Thus B is isomorphic to E_6 in low degrees.

