hilbertSeries(NCRing) -- Computes the Hilbert series of an NCRing
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note hilbertSeries: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertSeries,
  * Usage: 
        hseries = hilbertSeries(A)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Order: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmOrder=>_pd_pd_pd
        _rp, => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity,
      * *note Reduce: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertSeries_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmReduce=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value false,
  * Outputs:
      * hseries, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 

Description
===========

This method computes the Hilbert series of a graded NCRing.  If the ring is
defined ober QQ or ZZ/p, and standard graded, it calls *note hilbertBergman:
hilbertBergman,.  Otherwise, if the ring is defined over a field (and
potentially not standard graded), then a basis is computed and the generating
function of the degrees of that basis is returned.  The degree to which one
computes the Hilbert series is controlled with the Order option. The output is
returned as a polynomial in ZZ[T].

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ{x,y,z}                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : NCPolynomialRing                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : hilbertSeries(A,Order=>10)                                              |
|                                                                             |
|                2      3      4       5       6        7        8         9  |
|o2 = 1 + 3T + 9T  + 27T  + 81T  + 243T  + 729T  + 2187T  + 6561T  + 19683T  +|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|           10                                                                |
|     59049T                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : ZZ[T]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : setWeights(A,{1,2,3})                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : NCPolynomialRing                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hilbertSeries(A,Order=>10)                                              |
|                                                                             |
|               2     3     4      5      6      7      8       9       10    |
|o4 = 1 + T + 2T  + 4T  + 7T  + 13T  + 24T  + 44T  + 81T  + 149T  + 274T      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : ZZ[T]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : B = threeDimSklyanin(QQ,{1,1,-1},{x,y,z})                               |
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.                                      |
|Complete!                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : NCQuotientRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : hilbertSeries(B,Order=>10)                                              |
|--Calling bergman for HS computation.                                        |
|Complete!                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|                2      3      4      5      6      7      8      9      10   |
|o6 = 1 + 3T + 6T  + 10T  + 15T  + 21T  + 28T  + 36T  + 45T  + 55T  + 66T     |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : ZZ[T]                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

