isHomogeneous(NCRingMap) -- Determines if an NCRingMap preserves the natural grading
************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isHomogeneous: (Macaulay2Doc)isHomogeneous,
  * Usage: 
        isHomogeneous f
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note NCRingMap: NCRingMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

This method returns true if the map f is degree 0; that is, if the generators
of the source of f are mapped to elements of the same degree in the target.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{w,x,y,z})    |
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.              |
|Complete!                                            |
|                                                     |
|o1 = A                                               |
|                                                     |
|o1 : NCQuotientRing                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : B = QQ{w,x,y,z}/ncIdeal{w*x+x*w,w*y+y*w,x*y+y*x}|
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.              |
|Complete!                                            |
|                                                     |
|o2 = B                                               |
|                                                     |
|o2 : NCQuotientRing                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = ncMap(B,A,gens B)                           |
|                                                     |
|o3 = NCRingMap B <--- A                              |
|                                                     |
|o3 : NCRingMap                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : isHomogeneous f                                 |
|                                                     |
|o4 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C = QQ{a,b,c}                                   |
|                                                     |
|o5 = C                                               |
|                                                     |
|o5 : NCPolynomialRing                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g = ncMap(C,A,{a^3,b^2,a+b,a-b})                |
|                                                     |
|o6 = NCRingMap C <--- A                              |
|                                                     |
|o6 : NCRingMap                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isHomogeneous g                                 |
|                                                     |
|o7 = false                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : setWeights(A,{3,2,1,1})                         |
|                                                     |
|o8 = A                                               |
|                                                     |
|o8 : NCQuotientRing                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : isHomogeneous g                                 |
|                                                     |
|o9 = true                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note isHomogeneous(NCIdeal): isHomogeneous_lpNCIdeal_rp, -- Determines
    whether the input defines a homogeneous object

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note isHomogeneous(NCRingMap): isHomogeneous_lpNCRingMap_rp, -- Determines
    if an NCRingMap preserves the natural grading
