isLeftRegular -- Determines if a given (homogeneous) element is regular in a given degree
*****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        isLeftRegular(x,n) or isRightRegular(x,n)
  * Inputs:
      * x, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement: NCRingElement,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the degree in which regularity
        is checked.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Given an element x in an NCRing, isLeftRegular returns true if a*x=0 implies
a=0 for all a in the specified homogeneous degree n. Likewise isRightRegular
returns true if x*a=0 implies a=0 for all elements a of degree n. The method
calls *note leftMultiplicationMap: leftMultiplicationMap, or *note
rightMultiplicationMap: leftMultiplicationMap, as appropriate and checks the
kernel in the specified degree.

+----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = threeDimSklyanin(QQ,{1,1,-1},{x,y,z})|
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.       |
|Complete!                                     |
|                                              |
|o1 = B                                        |
|                                              |
|o1 : NCQuotientRing                           |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : g = -y^3-x*y*z+y*x*z+x^3                 |
|                                              |
|       3          3                           |
|o2 = -y +yxz-xyz+x                            |
|                                              |
|o2 : B                                        |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : isLeftRegular(g,6)                       |
|                                              |
|o3 = true                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = QQ{x,y}                              |
|                                              |
|o4 = C                                        |
|                                              |
|o4 : NCPolynomialRing                         |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : D = C/ncIdeal{x^2+x*y,y^2}               |
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.       |
|Complete!                                     |
|                                              |
|o5 = D                                        |
|                                              |
|o5 : NCQuotientRing                           |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : isLeftRegular(x,1)                       |
|                                              |
|o6 = true                                     |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : isRightRegular(x,1)                      |
|                                              |
|o7 = false                                    |
+----------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note leftMultiplicationMap: leftMultiplicationMap, -- Computes a matrix
    for left or right multiplication by a homogeneous element
  * *note rightMultiplicationMap: leftMultiplicationMap, -- Computes a matrix
    for left or right multiplication by a homogeneous element

Ways to use isLeftRegular:
==========================

  * "isLeftRegular(NCRingElement,ZZ)"

For the programmer
==================

