ncMap -- Make a map to or from an NCRing
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        f = ncMap(B,A,m)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, or a *note Ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,
      * B, an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, or a *note Ring:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,
      * m, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the images of the generators of
        A.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Derivation => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value false
  * Outputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note NCRingMap: NCRingMap,, 

Description
===========

NCRingMaps are linear and multiplicative by definition, but need not be
well-defined or homogeneous. The user has the option to define an NCRingMap to
be a derivation. Such a map must have the same source and target.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{w,x,y,z})   |
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.             |
|Complete!                                           |
|                                                    |
|o1 = A                                              |
|                                                    |
|o1 : NCQuotientRing                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : B = QQ{a,b,c}                                  |
|                                                    |
|o2 = B                                              |
|                                                    |
|o2 : NCPolynomialRing                               |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = ncMap(B,A,{a^3,b^2,a+b,a-b})               |
|                                                    |
|o3 = NCRingMap B <--- A                             |
|                                                    |
|o3 : NCRingMap                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f(w*x+2*y)                                     |
|                                                    |
|         3 2                                        |
|o4 = 2b+a b +2a                                     |
|                                                    |
|o4 : B                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : g = ncMap(B,B,{a*b,b^2,c*a*c},Derivation=>true)|
|                                                    |
|o5 = NCRingMap B <--- B                             |
|                                                    |
|o5 : NCRingMap                                      |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g(a*b)==g(a)*b+a*g(b)                          |
|                                                    |
|o6 = true                                           |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : g(promote(1,B))                                |
|                                                    |
|o7 = 0                                              |
|                                                    |
|o7 : B                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : g(c*a+2*b)                                     |
|                                                    |
|                2                                   |
|o8 = caca+cab+2b                                    |
|                                                    |
|o8 : B                                              |
+----------------------------------------------------+

