NCMatrix -- Type of a matrix over a noncommutative ring
*******************************************************

Description
===========

This is the type of a matrix over a noncommutative ring.  These represent
homomorphisms between two free modules in chosen bases (whether you think of it
as a map of left or right modules is up you).  Modules themselves are not
implemented yet in the *note NCAlgebra: Top, package, but are slated for a
later release.

Common ways to make (and use) a matrix include

  * *note ncMatrix(List): ncMatrix, -- Create an NCMatrix
  * *note basis(ZZ,NCRing): basis_lpZZ_cmNCRing_rp, -- Returns a basis of an
    NCRing in a particular degree.
  * *note rightKernel(NCMatrix,ZZ): rightKernel, -- Method for computing
    kernels of matrices over noncommutative rings in a given degree without
    using Bergman
  * *note rightKernelBergman(NCMatrix): rightKernelBergman, -- Methods for
    computing kernels of matrices over noncommutative rings using Bergman

Common ways to get information about matrices

  * *note ring(NCMatrix): ring_lpNCMatrix_rp, -- Gives the ring of the NCMatrix
  * *note entries(NCMatrix): entries_lpNCMatrix_rp, -- Returns the entries of
    the NCMatrix

Common operations on matrices:

  * *note NCMatrix + NCMatrix: NCMatrix + NCMatrix, -- Add NCMatrices
  * *note NCMatrix - NCMatrix: NCMatrix - NCMatrix, -- Subtract NCMatrices
  * *note NCMatrix % NCGroebnerBasis: NCMatrix % NCGroebnerBasis, -- Reduces
    the entries of an NCMatrix with respect to an NCGroebnerBasis
  * *note NCMatrix * NCMatrix: NCMatrix _st NCMatrix, -- Product of NCMatrices
  * *note NCMatrix * NCRingElement: NCMatrix _st NCRingElement, -- Product of
    NCMatrices
  * *note NCMatrix * RingElement: NCMatrix _st RingElement, -- Product of
    NCMatrices
  * *note NCMatrix // NCMatrix: NCMatrix // NCMatrix, -- Factor one map through
    another
  * *note NCMatrix _ List: NCMatrix _us List, -- Select some columns of an
    NCMatrix
  * *note NCMatrix == NCMatrix: NCMatrix == NCMatrix, -- Test equality of
    matrices
  * *note NCMatrix | NCMatrix: NCMatrix | NCMatrix, -- Join NCMatrices
    horizontally
  * *note NCMatrix || NCMatrix: NCMatrix || NCMatrix, -- Join NCMatrices
    vertically
  * *note NCMatrix ^ List: NCMatrix ^ List, -- Select some rows of an NCMatrix
  * *note NCMatrix ^ ZZ: NCMatrix ^ ZZ, -- Exponentiate an NCMatrix

This is the type of a matrix with entries in an NCRing.  Many of the basic
operations one can perform on a *note Matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix, are also
allowed with an *note NCMatrix: NCMatrix,, and the behavior of the functions
should be similar to the corresponding 'usual' command. Some examples of
creating and using NCMatrices are given below.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ{a,b,c,d}                                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = A                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : NCPolynomialRing                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : M = ncMatrix {{a,b,c,d}}                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | a b c d |                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : NCMatrix                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : N = ncMatrix {{M,2*M,3*M},{4*M,5*M,6*M}}                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | a   b   c   d   2*a 2*b 2*c 2*d 3*a 3*b 3*c 3*d |                     |
|     | 4*a 4*b 4*c 4*d 5*a 5*b 5*c 5*d 6*a 6*b 6*c 6*d |                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : NCMatrix                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : B = QQ{x,y,z}                                                           |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : NCPolynomialRing                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f = y*z + z*y - x^2                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|            2                                                                |
|o5 = zy+yz-x                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : B                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : g = x*z + z*x - y^2                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|         2                                                                   |
|o6 = zx-y +xz                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : B                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
