NCRingElement % NCGroebnerBasis -- Reduces a NCRingElement by a NCGroebnerBasis
*******************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note %: (Macaulay2Doc)%,
  * Usage: 
        fred = f % Igb
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement: NCRingElement,, or an
        integer, or a rational number
      * Igb, an instance of the type *note NCGroebnerBasis: NCGroebnerBasis,, 
  * Outputs:
      * fred, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement: NCRingElement,, 

Description
===========

This command reduces the input modulo a noncommutative Groebner basis. It will
either reduce it using top-level Macaulay code, or via a call to Bergman,
depending on the size and degree of the input element.

+---------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ{x,y,z}                                 |
|                                                   |
|o1 = A                                             |
|                                                   |
|o1 : NCPolynomialRing                              |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : p = y*z + z*y - x^2                           |
|                                                   |
|            2                                      |
|o2 = zy+yz-x                                       |
|                                                   |
|o2 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : q = x*z + z*x - y^2                           |
|                                                   |
|         2                                         |
|o3 = zx-y +xz                                      |
|                                                   |
|o3 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : r = z^2 - x*y - y*x                           |
|                                                   |
|      2                                            |
|o4 = z -yx-xy                                      |
|                                                   |
|o4 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : I = ncIdeal {p,q,r}                           |
|                                                   |
|                             2      2      2       |
|o5 = Two-sided ideal {zy+yz-x , zx-y +xz, z -yx-xy}|
|                                                   |
|o5 : NCIdeal                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Igb = ncGroebnerBasis I                       |
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.            |
|Complete!                                          |
|                                                   |
|      2    2                2                      |
|o6 = y x-xy ; Lead Term = (y x, 1)                 |
|       2  2                  2                     |
|     yx -x y; Lead Term = (yx , 1)                 |
|         2                                         |
|     zx-y +xz; Lead Term = (zx, 1)                 |
|            2                                      |
|     zy+yz-x ; Lead Term = (zy, 1)                 |
|      2                      2                     |
|     z -yx-xy; Lead Term = (z , 1)                 |
|                                                   |
|o6 : NCGroebnerBasis                               |
+---------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : z^6 % Igb                                     |
|                                                   |
|                     2   2   3 3                   |
|o7 = yxyxyx+xyxyxy+3x yxy +3x y                    |
|                                                   |
|o7 : A                                             |
+---------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note NCRingElement % NCGroebnerBasis: NCRingElement % NCGroebnerBasis, --
    Reduces a NCRingElement by a NCGroebnerBasis
  * "QQ % NCGroebnerBasis"
  * "ZZ % NCGroebnerBasis"
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

