NCRingMap -- Type of a map to or from a noncommutative ring.
************************************************************

Description
===========

As in the commutative case, a map F:R->S where R or S is an NCRing is specified
by giving the images in S of the variables of R. The target map is given first.

Common ways to make (and use) an NCRingMap include

  * *note ncMap(Ring,NCRing,List): ncMap, -- Make a map to or from an NCRing
  * *note ncMap(NCRing,Ring,List): ncMap, -- Make a map to or from an NCRing
  * *note ncMap(NCRing,NCRing,List): ncMap, -- Make a map to or from an NCRing
  * *note normalElements(NCRingMap,ZZ): normalElements_lpNCRingMap_cmZZ_rp, --
    Finds elements normalized by a ring map
  * *note oreExtension(NCRing,NCRingMap,NCRingMap,NCRingElement): oreExtension,
    -- Creates an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreExtension(NCRing,NCRingMap,NCRingMap,Symbol): oreExtension, --
    Creates an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreExtension(NCRing,NCRingMap,NCRingElement): oreExtension, --
    Creates an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreExtension(NCRing,NCRingMap,Symbol): oreExtension, -- Creates an
    Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreIdeal(NCRing,NCRingMap,NCRingMap,NCRingElement): oreIdeal, --
    Creates the defining ideal of an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreIdeal(NCRing,NCRingMap,NCRingMap,Symbol): oreIdeal, -- Creates the
    defining ideal of an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreIdeal(NCRing,NCRingMap,NCRingElement): oreIdeal, -- Creates the
    defining ideal of an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
  * *note oreIdeal(NCRing,NCRingMap,Symbol): oreIdeal, -- Creates the defining
    ideal of an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring

Common ways to get information about NCRingMaps Code UL {TO (source,NCRingMap),
TO (target,NCRingMap), TO (matrix,NCRingMap), TO (isWellDefined,NCRingMap), TO
(isHomogeneous,NCRingMap), TO (symbol _, NCRingMap, ZZ)} Text Common operations
involving NCRingMaps Code UL {TO (ambient,NCRingMap), TO (symbol
/,List,NCRingMap), TO (symbol SPACE, NCRingMap, NCRingElement), TO (symbol
SPACE, NCRingMap, RingElement), TO (symbol SPACE, NCRingMap, NCMatrix), }

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{w,x,y,z})|
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.          |
|Complete!                                        |
|                                                 |
|o1 = A                                           |
|                                                 |
|o1 : NCQuotientRing                              |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : B = QQ{a,b,c}                               |
|                                                 |
|o2 = B                                           |
|                                                 |
|o2 : NCPolynomialRing                            |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : f = ncMap(B,A,{a^3,b^2,a+b,a-b})            |
|                                                 |
|o3 = NCRingMap B <--- A                          |
|                                                 |
|o3 : NCRingMap                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : target f                                    |
|                                                 |
|o4 = B                                           |
|                                                 |
|o4 : NCPolynomialRing                            |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : source f                                    |
|                                                 |
|o5 = A                                           |
|                                                 |
|o5 : NCQuotientRing                              |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : matrix f                                    |
|                                                 |
|o6 = | a^3 b^2 b+a -b+a |                        |
|                                                 |
|o6 : NCMatrix                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Note that NCRingMaps need not be well-defined or homogeneous. Apply a function
to an element or a matrix using the usual function notation. NCRingMaps are
linear and multiplicative by definition.

+--------------------+
|i7 : f(w*x+2*y)     |
|                    |
|         3 2        |
|o7 = 2b+a b +2a     |
|                    |
|o7 : B              |
+--------------------+
|i8 : isWellDefined f|
|                    |
|o8 = false          |
+--------------------+
|i9 : isHomogeneous f|
|                    |
|o9 = false          |
+--------------------+

The user has the option to define an NCRingMap to be a derivation. Of course,
such a map must have the same source and target.

+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : g = ncMap(B,B,{a*b,b^2,c*a*c},Derivation=>true)|
|                                                     |
|o10 = NCRingMap B <--- B                             |
|                                                     |
|o10 : NCRingMap                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : g(a*b)==g(a)*b+a*g(b)                          |
|                                                     |
|o11 = true                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : g(promote(1,B))                                |
|                                                     |
|o12 = 0                                              |
|                                                     |
|o12 : B                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : g(c*a+2*b)                                     |
|                                                     |
|                 2                                   |
|o13 = caca+cab+2b                                    |
|                                                     |
|o13 : B                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

