NCRingMap NCIdeal -- Apply a ring map to the generators of an ideal
*******************************************************************

  * Operator: *note SPACE: (Macaulay2Doc)SPACE,
  * Usage: 
        J = f I
  * Inputs:
      * f, an instance of the type *note NCRingMap: NCRingMap,, 
      * I, an instance of the type *note NCIdeal: NCIdeal,, or *note
        NCGroebnerBasis: NCGroebnerBasis,
  * Outputs:
      * J, an instance of the type *note NCIdeal: NCIdeal,, or *note
        NCGroebnerBasis: NCGroebnerBasis,

Description
===========

This function applies the ring map f to the generators of the ideal or
noncommutative Groebner basis that is passed in.

+------------------------------+
|i1 : A = QQ{x,y}              |
|                              |
|o1 = A                        |
|                              |
|o1 : NCPolynomialRing         |
+------------------------------+
|i2 : g = ncMap(A,A,{y,x})     |
|                              |
|o2 = NCRingMap A <--- A       |
|                              |
|o2 : NCRingMap                |
+------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ncIdeal {x^2*y+y*x^2}|
|                              |
|                        2  2  |
|o3 = Two-sided ideal {yx +x y}|
|                              |
|o3 : NCIdeal                  |
+------------------------------+
|i4 : g I                      |
|                              |
|                       2    2 |
|o4 = Two-sided ideal {y x+xy }|
|                              |
|o4 : NCIdeal                  |
+------------------------------+

