oreIdeal -- Creates the defining ideal of an Ore extension of a noncommutative ring
***********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        oreIdeal(A,sigma,delta,x) or oreIdeal(A,sigma,x)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, 
      * sigma, an instance of the type *note NCRingMap: NCRingMap,, 
      * delta, an instance of the type *note NCRingMap: NCRingMap,, 
      * x, an instance of the type *note NCRingElement: NCRingElement,, or a
        *note Symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Degree (missing documentation) => ..., default value 1, 
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note NCIdeal: NCIdeal,, 

Description
===========

Given a ring A, an Ore extension of A by x is the quotient of the free
extension A<x> by the relations x*a - sigma(a)*x-delta(a) where sigma is an
automorphism of A and delta is a sigma-derivation. This method returns the
defining ideal (in the appropriate tensor algebra) of an Ore extension of A by
x. The current version assumes the sigma-derivation delta is 0.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = skewPolynomialRing(QQ,(-1)_QQ,{x,y,z,w})                            |
|--Calling Bergman for NCGB calculation.                                      |
|Complete!                                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = B                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : NCQuotientRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : sigma = ncMap(B,B,{y,z,w,x})                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = NCRingMap B <--- B                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : NCRingMap                                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = oreIdeal(B,sigma,a)                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = Two-sided ideal {yx+xy, zx+xz, zy+yz, wx+xw, wy+yw, wz+zw, ax-ya, ay-za,|
|                                                                             |
|o3 : NCIdeal                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|az-wa, aw-xa}                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note oreExtension: oreExtension, -- Creates an Ore extension of a
    noncommutative ring

