setWeights -- Set a nonstandard grading for a NCRing.
*****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        setWeights(A,degList)
  * Inputs:
      * A, an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, 
      * degList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of integer weights
        to be assigned to the generators of A
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note NCRing: NCRing,, 

Description
===========

This method enables the user to work with rings which are not naturally graded
(the generators are not all degree 1). The user should be aware that  methods
which call Bergman may not work with nonstandard gradings. Perhaps the most
important example is hilbertBergman, which throws an error. Instead, use *note
hilbertSeries: (Macaulay2Doc)hilbertSeries,.

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : A=QQ{x,y,z}                     |
|                                     |
|o1 = A                               |
|                                     |
|o1 : NCPolynomialRing                |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : w=x^3-y^2                       |
|                                     |
|       2  3                          |
|o2 = -y +x                           |
|                                     |
|o2 : A                               |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : isHomogeneous w                 |
|                                     |
|o3 = false                           |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : setWeights(A, {2,3,1})          |
|                                     |
|o4 = A                               |
|                                     |
|o4 : NCPolynomialRing                |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : isHomogeneous w                 |
|                                     |
|o5 = true                            |
+-------------------------------------+
